        <Sticky classid="Sticky" id="975503493" x="0" y="162" w="360" h="468" colors="0, 15792890" layer="">
          <paramlist>
            <param name="font" value="1" />
            <param name="align" value="0" />
            <param name="style" value="1" />
            <param name="fg_color" value="0" />
            <param name="bg_color" value="15792890" />
            <param name="arrows" value="0" />
            <param name="opacity" value="25" />
            <param name="fg_color_adv" value="#FF000000" />
            <param name="bg_color_adv" value="#FFFAFAF0" />
            <param name="hl_color_adv" value="#FFFFFF00" />
            <param name="bdr_color_adv" value="#FF95918C" />
            <param name="full_font" value="Tahoma, 11world" />
          </paramlist><![CDATA[This PSCAD/EMTDC model implements a Type-4 WF based on a permanent magnet synchronous generator (PMSG) and a full-scale back-to-back voltage-source converter (VSC), comprising machine-side (MSC) and grid-side (GSC) converter controls. 

The Type-4 wind turbine model follows the PSCAD reference architecture: https://www.pscad.com/knowledge-base/article/227

The WF is integrated into the IEEE 39-bus benchmark system through a dedicated WF–grid integration link. The link reactance can be varied to modify the short-circuit ratio (SCR) at the PCC, enabling systematic investigation of weak-grid-induced subsynchronous oscillations (WG-PMSG-SSOs) under different network-strength conditions.

Current configuration: The WF replaces the SG at Bus 33 as an illustrative integration scenario. Other integration locations can be configured as required for different study cases.

Research purpose: To provide a reproducible EMT benchmark capable of generating WG-PMSG-SSOs for a broad range of research applications, including oscillation characterization, mechanism analysis, detection, localization, stability assessment, and mitigation/control strategy development.

Associated paper: 
T. Zamzam, Y. Qiblawey, A. Alassi, H. Abu-Rub, A. Massoud and A. Ghrayeb, "A Network-Side Assessment Framework and Benchmark System for Weak-Grid PMSG-Based Subsynchronous Oscillations," in IEEE Open Journal of the Industrial Electronics Society, vol. 7, pp. 1401-1420, 2026, doi: 10.1109/OJIES.2026.3724912.
]]></Sticky>
